---
import ToolingLayout from "../../layouts/ToolingLayout.astro";
import CopyableCode from "../../components/CopyableCode.astro";
import { InsetText } from "@i-dot-ai-npm/component-library-solid";
---

<ToolingLayout title="Set up Claude Code" currentPath="/tooling/claude-code">
  <h1 class="govuk-heading-xl">Set up Claude Code</h1>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    You can use the AI Gateway with Claude Code in your terminal, or as an
    extension in VS Code. It can only access Claude models.
  </p>

  <figure class="govuk-!-margin-bottom-6">
    <img
      src="/assets/images/gateway-diagram-claude-code.svg"
      alt="Diagram showing Claude Code running in the terminal or as an extension in VS Code. It connects to the AI Gateway, which provides access to Claude models."
      class="govuk-!-width-full"
    />
  </figure>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    Before you start, make sure you have{" "}
    <a class="govuk-link" href="/tooling/get-your-key">
      your AI Gateway key
    </a>
    . Then, to set Claude Code, you need to:
  </p>
  <ol class="govuk-list govuk-list--number">
    <li>
      <a class="govuk-link" href="#use-admin-permissions">
        Use admin permissions
      </a>
    </li>
    <li>
      <a class="govuk-link" href="#connect-to-github">
        Connect to GitHub (and install Xcode tools)
      </a>
    </li>
    <li>
      <a class="govuk-link" href="#install-claude-code">
        Install Claude Code
      </a>
    </li>
    <li>
      <a class="govuk-link" href="#install-vs-code">
        Install VS Code
      </a>
    </li>
    <li>
      (If needed){" "}
      <a class="govuk-link" href="#add-your-key">
        Add or renew your AI Gateway key
      </a>
    </li>
  </ol>

  <InsetText>
    These steps work for most setups. If you run into issues you can't resolve,
    contact us in the #ai-model-gateway-team channel on i.AI Slack.
  </InsetText>

  <h2 class="govuk-heading-l" id="use-admin-permissions">
    Use admin permissions
  </h2>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    You need (temporary) admin permissions to install software on your Mac.
  </p>

  <ol class="govuk-list govuk-list--number">
    <li>
      Select the padlock icon (<strong>Local Admin Management</strong>) on the
      top menu bar.
    </li>
    <li>
      Choose <strong>Install an app</strong>.
    </li>
    <li>
      Select <strong>Start session</strong>, and enter your laptop password.
    </li>
    <li>
      Select <strong>OK</strong>.
    </li>
  </ol>

  <InsetText>
    These permissions last for 10 minutes. Select the padlock to request more
    time.
  </InsetText>

  <h2 class="govuk-heading-l" id="connect-to-github">
    Connect to GitHub (and install Xcode tools)
  </h2>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    You need to connect to GitHub to quickly install our agents and skills, and
    to use GitHub with apps such as VS Code.
  </p>

  <ol class="govuk-list govuk-list--number">
    <li>
      To check if you have Xcode tools installed, in Terminal, run:
      <CopyableCode code="xcode-select --version" />
    </li>
    <li>
      If the command is not found, you need to install Xcode tools. To install
      Xcode tools, in Terminal, run:
      <CopyableCode code="xcode-select --install" />
    </li>
    <li>
      To connect your name to GitHub, in Terminal, run:
      <CopyableCode code='git config --global user.name "<Your Name>"' />
      <p class="govuk-body">
        where <code class="app-code app-code--variable">&lt;Your Name&gt;</code>{" "}
        is your name.
      </p>
    </li>
    <li>
      To connect your GitHub email, in Terminal, run:
      <CopyableCode code="git config --global user.email <your-email@example.com>" />
      <p class="govuk-body">
        where{" "}
        <code class="app-code app-code--variable">
          &lt;your-email@example.com&gt;
        </code>{" "}
        is the email you use to log into GitHub.
      </p>
    </li>
    <li>
      To generate an SSH key, in Terminal, run:
      <CopyableCode code="ssh-keygen -t ed25519" />
    </li>
    <li>
      When it says{" "}
      <code class="app-code">Enter file in which to save the key</code>, press
      return.
    </li>
    <li>
      When it says{" "}
      <code class="app-code">Enter passphrase (empty for no passphrase)</code>,
      press return twice.
    </li>
    <li>
      To show your SSH key, run:
      <CopyableCode code="cat ~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub" />
    </li>
    <li>
      Highlight the full line starting{" "}
      <code class="app-code">ssh-ed25519...</code> and copy it.
    </li>
    <li>
      To add your SSH key to GitHub, open{" "}
      <a
        class="govuk-link"
        href="https://github.com/settings/keys"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
      >
        GitHub SSH Settings
      </a>
      .
    </li>
    <li>
      Select <strong>New SSH key</strong>.
    </li>
    <li>
      In <strong>Title</strong>, add: <code class="app-code">Dev laptop</code>.
    </li>
    <li>
      In <strong>Key</strong>, paste your copied SSH key.
    </li>
    <li>
      Choose <strong>Add SSH key</strong>.
    </li>
    <li>
      To test that your SSH key is set up correctly with GitHub, in Terminal,
      run:
      <CopyableCode code="ssh -T git@github.com" />
    </li>
    <li>
      To confirm you trust the fingerprint (and want to continue), run:
      <CopyableCode code="yes" />
    </li>
  </ol>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    If you're set up correctly, Terminal will say:{" "}
    <code class="app-code">
      Hi &lt;username&gt;! You've successfully authenticated, but GitHub does
      not provide shell access.
    </code>
  </p>

  <h2 class="govuk-heading-l" id="install-claude-code">
    Install Claude Code
  </h2>

  <ol class="govuk-list govuk-list--number">
    <li>
      To install Claude Code, in Terminal, run:
      <CopyableCode code="brew install --cask claude-code" />
    </li>
    <li>
      To navigate to your Documents folder, run:
      <CopyableCode code="cd Documents" />
    </li>
    <li>
      To make a folder for your files, run:
      <CopyableCode code="mkdir <folder-name>" />
      <p class="govuk-body">
        where{" "}
        <code class="app-code app-code--variable">&lt;folder-name&gt;</code> is
        the name of your new folder.
      </p>
    </li>
    <li>
      To open your new folder, run:
      <CopyableCode code="cd <folder-name>" />
    </li>
    <li>
      To copy the configuration files from GitHub, run:
      <CopyableCode code="git clone git@github.com:i-dot-ai/coding-agent-litellm-config.git" />
    </li>
    <li>
      To open the configuration folder, run:
      <CopyableCode code="cd coding-agent-litellm-config" />
    </li>
    <li>
      To configure Claude Code, run:
      <CopyableCode code="./install.sh" />
    </li>
    <li>
      When it asks for your AI Gateway key, paste your key or press return to
      skip and add your key later.
    </li>
    <li>
      To go to your home folder, run:
      <CopyableCode code="cd" />
    </li>
    <li>
      To make a safe folder to use Claude in, run:
      <CopyableCode code="mkdir <folder-name>" />
      <p class="govuk-body">
        where{" "}
        <code class="app-code app-code--variable">&lt;folder-name&gt;</code> is
        the name of your new folder.
      </p>
    </li>
    <li>
      To open your new folder, run:
      <CopyableCode code="cd <folder-name>" />
    </li>
    <li>
      To start Claude, run:
      <CopyableCode code="claude" />
    </li>
    <li>
      Use the arrow keys to choose your preferred code formatting, and press
      return.
    </li>
    <li>
      Use the arrow keys to choose{" "}
      <code class="app-code">Yes, I trust this folder</code>, and press return.
    </li>
  </ol>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    The installer also registers a hook so Claude Code checks for config updates
    on each new session, and preserves any of your own hooks, plugins or env
    vars already in <code class="app-code">~/.claude/settings.json</code>. See
    the{" "}
    <a
      class="govuk-link"
      href="https://github.com/i-dot-ai/coding-agent-litellm-config"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener noreferrer"
    >
      coding-agent-litellm-config README
    </a>{" "}
    for full setup details, including rollback and uninstall instructions.
  </p>

  <h2 class="govuk-heading-l" id="install-vs-code">
    Install VS Code
  </h2>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    VS Code is an integrated development environment which lets you open files
    from the Terminal window.
  </p>

  <ol class="govuk-list govuk-list--number">
    <li>
      To check if you have VS Code installed, in Terminal, run:
      <CopyableCode code="code" />
    </li>
    <li>
      If the command is not found, you need to install VS Code. To install VS
      Code, in Terminal, run:
      <CopyableCode code="brew install --cask visual-studio-code" />
    </li>
  </ol>

  <h2 class="govuk-heading-l" id="add-your-key">
    Add or renew your AI Gateway key
  </h2>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    If you skipped adding your key during install, or need to replace an expired
    one, edit <code class="app-code">~/.claude/settings.json</code> directly:
  </p>

  <ol class="govuk-list govuk-list--number">
    <li>
      Copy your AI Gateway key (
      <a class="govuk-link" href="/tooling/get-your-key">
        how to get your key
      </a>
      ).
    </li>
    <li>
      In Terminal, run:
      <CopyableCode code="code ~/.claude/settings.json" />
    </li>
    <li>
      Inside the <code class="app-code">"env"</code> block, after{" "}
      <code class="app-code">"CLAUDE_CODE_SKIP_BEDROCK_AUTH": "1"</code>, add
      (or replace):
      <CopyableCode code={`"ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN": "<your-ai-gateway-key>",`} />
      <p class="govuk-body">
        where{" "}
        <code class="app-code app-code--variable">
          &lt;your-ai-gateway-key&gt;
        </code>{" "}
        is your API key.
      </p>
    </li>
    <li>Save the file.</li>
  </ol>
</ToolingLayout>
